Subject: [PATCH] compose: build the device profile inside the browser

The browser composes the device profile itself from a seed, the compiled
option tables and what the host can serve. Each value is drawn by
SHA-256 from its own labelled substream, so adding an option to the
tables does not change any other value an existing seed produces.
Options the host cannot back, such as more cores or memory than it has,
are filtered out before the draw, and a value with no option the host
can back is left to the host. A bare launch draws a fresh seed each
time, and --fingerprint=<seed> reproduces one device. The GPU cluster
comes from those the host's graphics backend can serve, and
--fingerprint-explain prints how it chose each value.

diff --git a/base/BUILD.gn b/base/BUILD.gn
index 87e4cdc..f29dfe9 100644
